            "id": "s1:p1",
            "text": "{{Expand Spanish|topic=scitech|Guarianthe aurantiaca|date=December 2009}}"
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p2",
            "text": "Guarianthe aurantiaca is a species of orchid. It is widespread across much of Mexico, south to Costa Rica. The diploid chromosome number of G. aurantiaca has been determined as 2n = 40."
          },
          {
            "id": "s1:p3",
            "text": "The phananthrenoids orchinol and loroglossol have a phytoalexin effect and reduce the growth of G. aurantiaca seedlings."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
